The companion JONSWAP heave difference is +0.036 percentage points of $H_s$ (paired-bootstrap 95\% interval [+0.030, +0.042]; paired Student-$t$ interval [+0.029, +0.043]). The exact sign and sign-flip $p$-values are 0.0020 and 0.0020, respectively. OU--III has lower mean normalized heave error in this ensemble.
These are ten paired seed differences, not forty independent seas.
